      "committer": {
        "name": "marc infield",
        "email": "marc@infield.net",
        "date": "2026-11-10T17:21:03Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(machines): Sienci AltMill 2x4, 4x4 and 4x8 on the grblHAL post\n\nThree built-in machines for Sienci's AltMill routers (SLB-EXT, grblHAL),\nposting through grblhal.cps - no AltMill post file. Figures from Sienci's\nspec pages; the 4x4's travel, rates, homing and spindle range from an\nAltMill 4x4's own $$ settings. safe_retract 0.0: the AltMill homes with\nmachine origin 0 at the homed top, so each tool change lifts G53 G0 Z0,\nthen T<n> M6 stands alone for gSender/ncSender or the ATC to take over.\n\nPinned by altmill_machines.rs and the 4x4 two-tool goldens (mm, inch).\nStacked on #715 (grblHAL post).\n\nFixes #728\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
